    <statement><p>State the type of the quadratic surface:</p>
<p><m>x^2 - \left( \frac{y}{5} \right)^2 + z^2=1</m></p>
<p>1. Hyperboloid of two sheets</p>
<p>2. Hyperboloid of one sheet</p>
<p>3. Ellipsoid</p>
<p>4. None of these</p>
<p><fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Describe the trace obtained by intersecting with the plane <m>y=0</m>:</p>
<p>1. Ellipse</p>
<p>2. Hyperbola</p>
<p>3. Circle</p>
<p>4. Empty set</p>
<p><fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>xz</m>-trace is obtained by substituting <m>y=0</m> in the equation. This gives the equation <m>x^2 + z^2=1</m> which defines a circle in the <m>xz</m>-plane.






</solution>
